EXT. ALPINE BIVOUAC LEDGE - NIGHT

A narrow shelf of rock, two thousand feet above a sleeping valley. Snow hisses against a tiny orange tent pitched at an angle that argues with gravity. A stove burns blue.

LUCIEN DUMONT, forties, bearded, ice in his moustache, stirs a pot of soup. Beside him, ODALYS FERRAND, thirties, wrapped in a sleeping bag, her knees drawn up, sips from a battered tin mug.

ODALYS
It's quiet, Lucien.

LUCIEN
Too quiet, Oddy?

ODALYS
No. Just quiet.

LUCIEN
Good. We deserve it.

He ladles soup into her mug. She smiles, small and grateful. They sit watching the stars come out above the ridge. Far below, tiny lights flicker in a village.

ODALYS
Tomorrow, the summit.

LUCIEN
Tomorrow, the summit.

ODALYS
And a hot bath.

LUCIEN
And a hot bath.

She leans her head on his shoulder. He lets her. For a moment, nothing in the world is wrong.

Then a thin hiss. Not the stove. Odalys lifts her head. Lucien freezes, ladle in the air. Both listen. The ice above them creaks.

ODALYS
Lucien--

LUCIEN
Don't move.

They both look up. A crack runs across the overhang, bright and fine as a hair.

LUCIEN
We have to go.

ODALYS ^
We have to go.

They scramble. He grabs the rope, she grabs the pack. The tent lurches. Soup spills, hissing on the stove.

LUCIEN (CONT'D)
Clip in! Clip in, Oddy!

ODALYS
I'm clipped, I'm clipped!

They tumble out of the tent together and dive into the snow at the ledge's edge as the overhang breaks free and thunders past. The tent is gone in a white roar.

The avalanche dies into silence. They lie panting, tangled in the rope, their breath mingling in clouds.

ODALYS (CONT'D)
(a shaky laugh)
Well. That was quiet.

LUCIEN
(laughs too)
Very.
